cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "UStore: GPU-Accelerated Multi-Modal Transactional Database Engine Built around Kernel Bypass"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: https://github.com/unum-cloud/UStore
url: https://www.unum.cloud/ustore
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.7537042
abstract: >-
  UStore is an embedded transactional database engine that keeps blobs, documents, graphs, strings
  and markup pages in collections addressed by 128-bit UUID keys, with transactions spanning
  collections behind one engine-agnostic C ABI. Its NVMe engine reaches drives through kernel
  bypass with io_uring and SPDK, lays immutable sorted runs into 1 GB slots of raw drives or into
  files under JSON manifests, searches them with SIMD S+ trees, and merges them on GPUs that read
  through GPUDirect Storage. It links into the process that uses it on machines pairing NVMe
  drives with GPUs, beside an in-memory reference engine and RocksDB and LevelDB engines that serve
  the same calls.
keywords:
  - database
  - transactions
  - key-value store
  - multi-modal
  - nvme
  - kernel bypass
  - gpu
  - log-structured merge tree

